{
  "title": "Child Improvement by Location and Coach",
  "subtitle": "Comparing baseline and endline metrics to show progress.",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Average Shuttle Run Improvement by Location",
      "sql": "SELECT b.Location, AVG(e.\"Shuttle run sec\" - b.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS avg_improvement FROM baseline b JOIN endline e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
      "x": "Location",
      "y": ["avg_improvement"],
      "unit": "seconds"
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Average Sit Ups Improvement by Coach",
      "sql": "SELECT b.Coach, AVG(e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\") AS avg_improvement FROM baseline b JOIN endline e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
      "x": "Coach",
      "y": ["avg_improvement"],
      "unit": "count"
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top 5 Locations with Highest Average Shuttle Run Improvement",
      "sql": "SELECT b.Location, AVG(e.\"Shuttle run sec\" - b.\"Shuttle run sec\") AS avg_improvement FROM baseline b JOIN endline e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 5",
      "columns": [
        {"name": "Location"},
        {"name": "avg_improvement", "unit": "seconds"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top 5 Coaches with Highest Average Sit Ups Improvement",
      "sql": "SELECT b.Coach, AVG(e.\"Sit ups\" - b.\"Sit ups\") AS avg_improvement FROM baseline b JOIN endline e ON b.\"Child ID\" = e.\"Child ID\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 5",
      "columns": [
        {"name": "Coach"},
        {"name": "avg_improvement", "unit": "count"}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "The dashboard presents two primary metrics of child improvement: average shuttle run time reduction and average increase in sit-ups. Panel p1 visualizes how different locations contributed to faster shuttle run times, with the most improvement highlighted at the top. Panel p2 shows which coaches were most effective in boosting sit-up counts across their groups. The table panels p3 and p4 list the top five locations and coaches, respectively, providing a quick reference for the most impactful areas. Observations should focus on the magnitude of improvement ({{p1}} and {{p2}}) and the consistency across locations and coaches, noting any outliers or patterns in the narrative."
}

{
  "title": "Donor Fitness Programme Results Summary",
  "subtitle": "Key outcomes and trends from baseline to endline assessments",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "kpi",
      "title": "Total children enrolled",
      "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM baseline",
      "unit": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "bar",
      "title": "Average shuttle run time by gender",
      "sql": "SELECT Gender, AVG(\"Shuttle run sec\") AS avg_shuttle FROM endline GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY avg_shuttle DESC",
      "x": "Gender",
      "y": ["avg_shuttle"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "line",
      "title": "Monthly sit-up improvement trend",
      "sql": "SELECT \"Child ID\", \"Sit ups\" AS start_situps, (SELECT \"Sit ups\" FROM endline e2 WHERE e2.\"Child ID\" = baseline.\"Child ID\") AS end_situps FROM baseline",
      "x": "\"Child ID\"",
      "y": ["end_situps - start_situps"]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "table",
      "title": "Top 5 coaches by average sit-up improvement",
      "sql": "SELECT Coach, AVG((SELECT \"Sit ups\" FROM endline e2 WHERE e2.\"Child ID\" = baseline.\"Child ID\") - baseline.\"Sit ups\") AS avg_improvement FROM baseline GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY avg_improvement DESC LIMIT 5"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": "The donor's fitness programme demonstrated notable improvements across key metrics. {{p1}} children participated, highlighting broad reach. Gender-wise, {{p2}} shows that {{p2}} on average completed the shuttle run faster post-programme, indicating enhanced agility. The line chart in {{p3}} reveals a consistent upward trend in sit-up performance, with an average increase of {{p3}} repetitions per child, underscoring the programme's effectiveness in building endurance. Finally, the table in {{p4}} identifies the top-performing coaches, with {{p4}} leading in average sit-up gains, suggesting targeted coaching strategies contributed significantly to outcomes. Overall, the data underscores the programme's success in fostering measurable fitness gains among participants."
}

